{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "AWS-0034",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "ECS clusters should have container insights enabled"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Cloudwatch Container Insights provide more metrics and logs for container based applications and micro services.\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0034",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration AWS-0034\nType: Terraform Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: ECS clusters should have container insights enabled\nMessage: Cluster does not have container insights enabled.\nLink: [AWS-0034](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0034)\nCloudwatch Container Insights provide more metrics and logs for container based applications and micro services.\n",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration AWS-0034**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Terraform Security Check|LOW|ECS clusters should have container insights enabled|Cluster does not have container insights enabled.|[AWS-0034](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0034)|\n\nCloudwatch Container Insights provide more metrics and logs for container based applications and micro services.\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-0025",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "DynamoDB tables should use at rest encryption with a Customer Managed Key"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Using AWS managed keys does not allow for fine grained control. DynamoDB tables are encrypted by default using AWS managed encryption keys. To increase control of the encryption and control the management of factors like key rotation, use a Customer Managed Key.\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0025",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration AWS-0025\nType: Terraform Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: DynamoDB tables should use at rest encryption with a Customer Managed Key\nMessage: Table encryption explicitly uses the default KMS key.\nLink: [AWS-0025](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0025)\nUsing AWS managed keys does not allow for fine grained control. DynamoDB tables are encrypted by default using AWS managed encryption keys. To increase control of the encryption and control the management of factors like key rotation, use a Customer Managed Key.\n",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration AWS-0025**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Terraform Security Check|LOW|DynamoDB tables should use at rest encryption with a Customer Managed Key|Table encryption explicitly uses the default KMS key.|[AWS-0025](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0025)|\n\nUsing AWS managed keys does not allow for fine grained control. DynamoDB tables are encrypted by default using AWS managed encryption keys. To increase control of the encryption and control the management of factors like key rotation, use a Customer Managed Key.\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-0098",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Secrets Manager should use customer managed keys"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Secrets Manager encrypts secrets by default using a default key created by AWS. To ensure control and granularity of secret encryption, CMK's should be used explicitly.\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0098",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration AWS-0098\nType: Terraform Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: Secrets Manager should use customer managed keys\nMessage: Secret explicitly uses the default key.\nLink: [AWS-0098](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0098)\nSecrets Manager encrypts secrets by default using a default key created by AWS. To ensure control and granularity of secret encryption, CMK's should be used explicitly.\n",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration AWS-0098**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Terraform Security Check|LOW|Secrets Manager should use customer managed keys|Secret explicitly uses the default key.|[AWS-0098](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0098)|\n\nSecrets Manager encrypts secrets by default using a default key created by AWS. To ensure control and granularity of secret encryption, CMK's should be used explicitly.\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-0133",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Enable Performance Insights to detect potential problems"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Enabling Performance insights allows for greater depth in monitoring data.\nFor example, information about active sessions could help diagose a compromise or assist in the investigation\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0133",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration AWS-0133\nType: Terraform Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: Enable Performance Insights to detect potential problems\nMessage: Instance does not have performance insights enabled.\nLink: [AWS-0133](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0133)\nEnabling Performance insights allows for greater depth in monitoring data.\nFor example, information about active sessions could help diagose a compromise or assist in the investigation\n",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration AWS-0133**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Terraform Security Check|LOW|Enable Performance Insights to detect potential problems|Instance does not have performance insights enabled.|[AWS-0133](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0133)|\n\nEnabling Performance insights allows for greater depth in monitoring data.\nFor example, information about active sessions could help diagose a compromise or assist in the investigation\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-0017",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CloudWatch log groups should be encrypted using CMK"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CloudWatch log groups are encrypted by default, however, to get the full benefit of controlling key rotation and other KMS aspects a KMS CMK should be used.\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0017",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration AWS-0017\nType: Terraform Plan Snapshot Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: CloudWatch log groups should be encrypted using CMK\nMessage: Log group is not encrypted.\nLink: [AWS-0017](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0017)\nCloudWatch log groups are encrypted by default, however, to get the full benefit of controlling key rotation and other KMS aspects a KMS CMK should be used.\n",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration AWS-0017**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Terraform Plan Snapshot Security Check|LOW|CloudWatch log groups should be encrypted using CMK|Log group is not encrypted.|[AWS-0017](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0017)|\n\nCloudWatch log groups are encrypted by default, however, to get the full benefit of controlling key rotation and other KMS aspects a KMS CMK should be used.\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.73.0"
        }
      },
